<% content_for :title, "Pricing — Anchor" %>

<%# Anchor has no billing system: it is MIT-licensed and self-hosted. This page
    says exactly that, and what the only real costs are (your own cloud). %>

<section class="pt-10 pb-8 text-center">
  <h1 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-[var(--anchor-text)] mb-2">
    Anchor is free and open source.
  </h1>
  <p class="text-sm text-[var(--anchor-muted)] max-w-xl mx-auto">
    MIT-licensed and self-hosted. There is no paid plan, no trial and no card.
    The only bill is the one from the cloud you deploy to — and the Local Docker provider costs nothing.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="pb-12">
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 max-w-4xl mx-auto">

    <div class="border-2 border-emerald-700/50 rounded-xl p-5 flex flex-col bg-emerald-950/10">
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-emerald-400 uppercase tracking-wide mb-3">Local Docker</p>
      <div class="flex items-end gap-1 mb-1">
        <span class="text-3xl font-bold text-[var(--anchor-text)]">$0</span>
      </div>
      <p class="text-xs text-[var(--anchor-muted)] mb-4">Try Anchor end-to-end on your laptop. No cloud account.</p>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-xs flex-1">
        <% ["Builds and runs apps on your local Docker daemon",
            "Framework detection + Dockerfile generation",
            "Live build logs, encrypted secrets",
            "Error categories and fix hints on failure"].each do |label| %>
          <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5 text-emerald-400 flex-shrink-0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/>
            </svg>
            <span class="text-[var(--anchor-text)]"><%= label %></span>
          </li>
        <% end %>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="border border-[var(--anchor-border)] rounded-xl p-5 flex flex-col">
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-[var(--anchor-muted)] uppercase tracking-wide mb-3">Google Cloud Run</p>
      <div class="flex items-end gap-1 mb-1">
        <span class="text-3xl font-bold text-[var(--anchor-text)]">$0</span>
        <span class="text-xs text-[var(--anchor-muted)] mb-1.5">+ your GCP bill</span>
      </div>
      <p class="text-xs text-[var(--anchor-muted)] mb-4">Deploy into your own GCP project. Google bills you directly, at Google's rates.</p>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-xs flex-1">
        <% ["Cloud Build + Artifact Registry + Cloud Run in your account",
            "Scale to zero: idle services cost nothing on Cloud Run",
            "Push-to-deploy via GitHub webhooks",
            "Set GCP budget alerts to cap spend"].each do |label| %>
          <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5 text-emerald-400 flex-shrink-0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/>
            </svg>
            <span class="text-[var(--anchor-text)]"><%= label %></span>
          </li>
        <% end %>
      </ul>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<div class="border-t border-[var(--anchor-border)]"></div>

<section class="py-12 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
  <p class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-widest text-[var(--anchor-muted)] uppercase text-center mb-8">Common questions</p>

  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-x-10 gap-y-7">
    <% [
      ["Is there a hosted version?",
       "No. You run Anchor yourself (bin/setup or docker compose up). It is the control plane; your apps run in your Docker or your cloud."],
      ["Will I get a surprise GCP bill?",
       "Cloud Run scales to zero, so idle apps cost nothing, but builds and traffic are billed by Google. Set a GCP budget alert before your first deploy."],
      ["Does Anchor store my code?",
       "No. The repo is cloned for the build and the working copy is deleted afterwards."],
      ["What does the AI explanation need?",
       "An API key for the configured model provider. Without one, failed deploys still get an error category and a rule-based fix hint."],
    ].each do |q, a| %>
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-[var(--anchor-text)] mb-1"><%= q %></h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-[var(--anchor-muted)] leading-relaxed"><%= a %></p>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="py-12 text-center border-t border-[var(--anchor-border)]">
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[var(--anchor-text)] mb-3">Run it locally in minutes.</h2>
  <p class="text-sm text-[var(--anchor-muted)] mb-6 max-w-md mx-auto">
    <code class="font-mono text-xs">git clone</code>, then <code class="font-mono text-xs">bin/setup</code> or
    <code class="font-mono text-xs">docker compose up</code>. A demo project is seeded for you.
  </p>
  <a href="https://github.com/nebullii/anchor" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
     class="inline-flex items-center gap-2.5 font-semibold text-sm px-6 py-2.5 rounded-lg transition-colors"
     style="background: var(--anchor-accent); color: var(--anchor-bg-1);">
    View the source on GitHub
  </a>
</section>
